+Migrations run as `neondb_owner`; the Workers connect as `project_name_app`, which reads and
+writes rows but cannot change the schema or `schema_migrations`. After migrating, every
+deploy runs `scripts/ensure-app-role.mjs`: it creates the role in SQL (a role Neon creates is
+always a member of `neon_superuser`), sets its password from the `DB_APP_PASSWORD` secret,
+re-grants it every table and sequence, and outputs the branch's connection string with the
+role's credentials swapped in. A table created outside a migration needs the next deploy, or
+a manual `GRANT`, before the Workers can use it.
 
